---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title={`Services · ${SITE_TITLE}`} description="Automation builds for small businesses. Lead follow-up, CRM logging, appointment workflows, and custom integrations." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="page-header">
				<p class="page-label">// SERVICES</p>
				<h1>What I build</h1>
				<p class="page-desc">
					I build workflow automations for small businesses. They run in the background
					and handle the repetitive stuff so your team doesn't have to.
				</p>
			</div>

			<section class="services">
				<div class="service-card">
					<p class="service-label">// 01</p>
					<h2>Lead follow-up automation</h2>
					<p>
						When a new lead comes in through your website, booking form, or ad platform, an automated
						message goes out within minutes. No manual work required. The lead hears from you while
						they're still thinking about you.
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Instant SMS or email reply on new inquiry</li>
						<li>Follow-up sequence if they don't respond</li>
						<li>Notification to you or your front desk</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<div class="service-card">
					<p class="service-label">// 02</p>
					<h2>CRM and booking log automation</h2>
					<p>
						New bookings, cancellations, and client notes flow into your CRM automatically.
						No copy-pasting, no forgetting to log. Your records stay clean without anyone managing them.
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Booking software to CRM sync</li>
						<li>Contact creation and updates</li>
						<li>Deal or pipeline stage updates on key events</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<div class="service-card">
					<p class="service-label">// 03</p>
					<h2>Appointment reminders and no-show recovery</h2>
					<p>
						Automated reminders before appointments reduce no-shows. When someone cancels or ghosts,
						a follow-up message goes out automatically to reschedule. You recover revenue without
						chasing people yourself.
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li>24-hour and 1-hour appointment reminders</li>
						<li>No-show and cancellation follow-up</li>
						<li>Rescheduling link or reply option</li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<div class="service-card">
					<p class="service-label">// 04</p>
					<h2>Custom integrations</h2>
					<p>
						Have two tools that don't talk to each other? Or a process that's mostly manual because
						there's no off-the-shelf solution? I'll build the connection. Most integrations are
						simpler than they look.
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li>Zapier replacement builds (usually faster and cheaper to run)</li>
						<li>Form-to-spreadsheet or form-to-CRM pipelines</li>
						<li>Internal notifications and Slack alerts</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="process">
				<p class="page-label">// PROCESS</p>
				<div class="process-steps">
					<div class="process-step">
						<span class="step-num">01</span>
						<div>
							<h3>Scoping call</h3>
							<p>We talk through what you're doing manually, what tools you're using, and what a working
							solution looks like. Free, no obligation.</p>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="process-step">
						<span class="step-num">02</span>
						<div>
							<h3>Build</h3>
							<p>I build it, test it against real scenarios, and document how it works. Most builds
							take less than a week.</p>
						</div>
					</div>
					<div class="process-step">
						<span class="step-num">03</span>
						<div>
							<h3>Handoff</h3>
							<p>You get a walkthrough, a Loom recording, and ongoing support if anything breaks
							or needs adjustment.</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="cta-block">
				<div class="cta-inner">
					<p class="page-label">// GET STARTED</p>
					<h2>Tell me what you're doing by hand.</h2>
					<p>If it happens repeatedly and follows a pattern, there's probably a way to automate it.
					Reach out and we'll figure out if it's worth building.</p>
					<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in touch</a>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	.page-header {
		margin-bottom: 3em;
	}

	.page-label {
		font-family: ui-monospace, 'Cascadia Code', 'Fira Mono', monospace;
		font-size: 0.78em;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		color: var(--moss);
		margin: 0 0 0.75em 0;
	}

	.page-header h1 {
		font-size: 2.4em;
		margin: 0 0 0.5em 0;
	}

	.page-desc {
		color: var(--silver);
		font-size: 0.95em;
		max-width: 560px;
		margin: 0;
		line-height: 1.75;
	}

	/* ── Service cards ─────────────────────────── */
	.services {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0;
		margin-bottom: 4em;
	}

	.service-card {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--bg-border);
		padding: 2em 0;
	}
	.service-card:last-child {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--bg-border);
	}

	.service-label {
		font-family: ui-monospace, 'Cascadia Code', 'Fira Mono', monospace;
		font-size: 0.75em;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		color: var(--moss);
		margin: 0 0 0.6em 0;
	}

	.service-card h2 {
		font-size: 1.25em;
		margin: 0 0 0.6em 0;
		color: var(--text);
	}

	.service-card > p {
		font-size: 0.95em;
		color: var(--silver);
		max-width: 620px;
		margin: 0 0 1em 0;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.service-card ul {
		margin: 0;
		padding-left: 1.25em;
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.3em;
	}

	.service-card li {
		font-size: 0.9em;
		color: var(--silver-light);
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	/* ── Process ───────────────────────────────── */
	.process {
		margin-bottom: 4em;
	}

	.process-steps {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1.5em;
	}

	.process-step {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1.5em;
		align-items: flex-start;
	}

	.step-num {
		font-family: ui-monospace, 'Cascadia Code', 'Fira Mono', monospace;
		font-size: 0.75em;
		color: var(--moss);
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		padding-top: 0.2em;
		flex-shrink: 0;
		width: 2em;
	}

	.process-step h3 {
		font-size: 1em;
		margin: 0 0 0.35em 0;
		color: var(--text);
	}

	.process-step p {
		font-size: 0.9em;
		color: var(--silver);
		margin: 0;
		line-height: 1.65;
	}

	/* ── CTA ───────────────────────────────────── */
	.cta-block {
		margin-bottom: 2em;
	}

	.cta-inner {
		background-color: var(--bg-surface);
		border: 1px solid var(--bg-border);
		border-radius: 8px;
		padding: 2.5em;
	}

	.cta-inner h2 {
		font-size: 1.5em;
		margin: 0 0 0.6em 0;
		color: var(--text);
	}

	.cta-inner p {
		font-size: 0.95em;
		color: var(--silver);
		max-width: 480px;
		margin: 0 0 1.5em 0;
		line-height: 1.7;
	}

	.btn {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 0.65em 1.4em;
		border-radius: 4px;
		font-size: 0.95em;
		font-weight: 600;
		cursor: pointer;
		text-decoration: none;
		transition: all 0.15s ease;
	}
	.btn:hover { text-decoration: none; }

	.btn-primary {
		background-color: var(--red);
		color: #FFFFFF;
	}
	.btn-primary:hover { background-color: var(--red-dark); }

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.cta-inner { padding: 1.5em; }
	}
</style>
